      },
      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "To cross breed bees you need two different species of bees. One drone and one princess from different naturally-generating hives (Meadows and Forest as an example).\n\nBee Houses do not allow crossbreeding. You need an Apiary to cross-breed them to a new species. Certain frames will help this process. Shortening their lifespan means faster crosses. Increasing the mutation rate means getting mutations and thus rare bees quicker.\n\nCommon Bees produce Honey Combs every 2.2 minutes. Note that production times are an approximation based on the bee\u0027s base production speed and the product\u0027s rarity. They do not reflect actual production time.\n\nMake sure your bees are pure by checking their genetics with a Beealyzer or GT scanner.\n\n[note]Breeder\u0027s Notes:\n\nRiiiight from the start, they have a trick for you. The Common bee is bred from most mundane species smashed into each other. The problem is the Cultivated species, which is next in line, is bred with most mundane species along with Common. Noble and Diligent then are crossed from Common and Cultivated. You could start with two mundane bees, have the results loop back unattended, and run that whole progression. Here\u0027s an example active:inactive mix you could get on a princess over time:\n\nMeadows:Forest\nMeadows:Common (Yay!)\nCommon:Meadows (Double yay! Active trait!)\nCultivated:Common (Boo!)\n. . . some time passes . . .\nDiligent:Noble (Wait, what?!)\n\nMeanwhile, this quest would still be sitting there, waiting for you to submit Common bees. Whoops!\n\nIf Cultivated starts to show up, just stuff any princesses and drones involved into a chest and act like that didn\u0027t happen for now. You can use them when you complete this quest to jumpstart the Cultivated species.\n\nNow, if you don\u0027t have any way to speed up breeding and don\u0027t want to stand around to micromanage, you can try filtering, or just checking on the result from time to time. Either way, maybe don\u0027t leave it going overnight if you\u0027re on a server.[/note]",
