      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Supporting circuit boards that can hold 4 electron tubes, the Electrical Stimulator provides a variety of functions. Use a Forestry Soldering Iron on an Intricate Circuit Board to set four slots worth of electron tubes. The tubes\u0027 capabilities are listed here as percentages:\n\nIron ET -\u003e +0.5 Production\nDiamantine ET -\u003e +1.5 Production\nApatine ET -\u003e 1.5x Pollination (Max 5x)\nObsidian ET -\u003e 0.8x Lifespan\nLapis ET -\u003e 1.5x Lifespan (Max 5x)\nBlazing ET -\u003e Simulates Hellish temperature\nGolden ET -\u003e 1.5x Mutation Rate (Max 5x)\nTin ET -\u003e 0.4x Territory (Min 0.1) \u0026 -0.1 Production\nBronze ET -\u003e 1.5x Territory (Max 5x)\n\nGenetic Decay is also increased by 50% for all of them. This affects how long until ignoble bees die off, so don\u0027t worry about it if your bees are pristine.\n\nRemember that lifespan is represented by ticks, not time. You need a world accelerator if you want a lifespan that is really less than 1 tick.\n\n[note]Breeder\u0027s Notes:\n12x Golden ETs and 20x Obsidian ETs across eight of these will make a super breeding party alveary; it will spike your mutation chances while dramatically decreasing lifespan. If you have been using the oblivion frame in an apiary to shorten lifespan for breeding, then this *does not* replace that because you cannot use world accelerators in alvearies. So the shortest you can reduce a bee\u0027s life cycle to is 1 tick \u003d 27 seconds. On the other hand, dramatically increasing the mutation rate in the alveary may be faster for crossbreeding.\n\nProduction Apiarist\u0027s Notes:\nAlternately, you can slam down three of these with:\n* 10x Diamantine\n* 2x Iron\nThat\u0027ll take you right up to the production limit. Any higher and you risk your pristine princesses turning ignoble from overwork.[/note]",
