      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The Acclimatiser can widen the temperature tolerance of a bee. This is technically a little side quest with Binnie\u0027s Genetics machines, but these alterations are permanent and carry into their genome.\n\nNote that the bee\u0027s species determines its favored temperature for jubilance. You can\u0027t use this to make a bee produce secondary products in a different climate.\n\nDrones, princesses, queens, and even larvae can go in these machines. This means you can boost one queen and be set for life for that bee.\n\n(You can also use it for pollen, butterflies, caterpillars, plants...)\n\nWhen a specimen\u0027s tolerance has been pushed as far as it can go, that bee will go in the output slot. The typical thing to do here is pipe the bee automatically into another Acclimatiser like a little trauma conga line. At the end, the bee should be able to tolerate being anywhere.\n\nHere\u0027s what you can use for what at what factors:\n* Temperature down\n  * ice: 0.75\n  * snowball: 0.15\n* Temperature up\n  * lava (canned!): 0.75\n  * blaze powder: 0.5\n  * blaze rod: 0.75\n* Humidity up:\n  * water (canned!): 0.75\n* Humidity down:\n  * sand: 0.15\n\nFluid containers are consumed. If only you had a waxy substance in overabundance you could use for throwaway fluids!\n\n[note]The Ole\u0027 \"Both Trick\": If your specimen already has at least Up/Down 1 for temperature or humidity, acclimatizing it in the opposite direction will make it Both 1. The trick is that it\u0027ll now grow both ways for the price of expanding only in one.\n\nSo, if handling canned water and lava is annoying, and you can start with Up 1 for temperature and humidity, then you can just bombard it with temperature and humidity lowering steps. It\u0027ll switch to Both 1 and then eventually Both 5 without ever raising temperature or humidity again.\n\nThis lets you skip out on canning liquids, you sly dog.\n[/note]",
