      "desc:8": "Tired of spamming Centrifuges already? \n\nAlas, with your newfound ZPM technology you can finally fabricate a Centrifuge with some real power; §5§lThe Spinmatron-2737§r!\n\nThe Spinmatron§r comes with a litany of advantages compared to the regular centrifuge multiblock, including a §2§l3x§r Speed boost, a §2§l30%§r reduction in EU usage, and a malleable number of parallels.\n\nUnlike the generic turbine that comes stock in a normal Centrifuge, the Spinmatron§r graciously allows you to choose the quality of the turbines that go into the machine. You can add between §9§l2-8§r turbines depending on the machine tier, each turbine will increase the parallel amount by [§94 * Turbine Material Tier§r]. §3(You\u0027ll want to avoid using smaller, non-huge turbines!)§r\n\nThis efficiency comes at a cost however, and will require [§9Recipe Tier * 10§r] L/s of §5Kerosene§r in order to run. This can optionally be switched out with §5Biocatalyzed Propulsion Fluid§r for a §2§l1.25x§r parallel multiplier once you\u0027ve reached §4UEV§r.\n\nAdditionally there are three modes that come unique to the Spinmatron:\n\n- §dLight§r -\u003e Gives increased speed in exchange for only being able to process [§9Voltage Tier - 3§r] recipes\n\n- §6Normal§r -\u003e No changes\n\n- §aHeavy§r -\u003e Grants the ability to craft Heavy Mode dependent recipes in exchange for reducing your parallels by §c§l32x§r and consuming §5Biocatalyzed Propulsion Fluid§r.\n\n[note]Checkout the tooltip for more information![/note]\n\n[warn]Use the GUI for adding turbines; don\u0027t add them to the rotor assemblies.[/warn]",
