      "desc:8": "The MKII is the penultimate upgrade in the Matter Manipulator line. It is much more powerful, storing §210x§r the power, with a range of §2128 Blocks§r, and the ability to place §2256 Blocks/Second§r. In addition to all of the MKI features you now unlock §5§ltwo powerful new modes§r:\n\n- §5§lCopy / Paste§r: Copy a selection of blocks and paste it as many times as you\u0027d like. Works best with GT \u0026 AE2.\n\n- §5§lMove§r: Similar to Copy / Paste, but will physically relocate something already built.\n\nHere is a short list of things that are copied / moved with the MM, the more complete list is on the Readme, but this should give you a general idea of how versatile it is.\n\n§3§lGregTech:§r\n- Pipe/Cable connections\n- Machine color\n- Machine front \u0026 output directions\n- Basic machine settings (auto outputs, etc)\n- Hatch settings (sorting, stack limiting, etc)\n- Multi machine settings (void protection, batch mode, etc)\n- Multi rotation\n- Covers\n- Strong redstone output\n- Custom names\n- Ghost circuits\n- Bus/hatch item/fluid lock\n- Modes (for machines that use the new mode system)\n- Data stick data\n- TecTech machine input parameters\n- ME output bus/hatch capacity\n\n§3§lAE2:§r\n- Any coloring\n- The orientation\n- The configuration\n- The upgrades\n- Custom names\n- Any stored cells (will also automatically configure cells \u0026 install their upgrades)\n- Any patterns (will encode but not decode patterns)\n- Priority Settings\n- P2P Settings\n- OreDict / Regular Filter\n\n§9§3§lAdvanced Copy Options:§r \n\nWhen in Copy / Paste mode, the radial menu has an §5§lAdvanced Options§r sub-menu with two powerful toggles:\n  - §5§l§5§lLink to External Hubs§r: When copying wireless connectors that are linked to a hub outside of the copy region, the pasted connectors will stay linked to that original hub.\n  - §5§lAuto-P2P Interfaces§r: Replaces ME Interfaces in the copied region with P2P ME tunnels, automatically placing matching tunnels at the source for seamless item routing.",
