      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The §5Ritual of Gaia\u0027s Transformation§r is the Blood Magic way of changing biomes. It consists of 116 Ritual Stones, including the Dusk ones, and requires an §9Awakened Activation Crystal§r.\n\nTo use the ritual, simply activate it, and it will transform an area up to §221x21§r.\n\nIf you want to change the biome you get from the ritual, use Arcane Plinths. The ritual starts from 0.5 humidity and 0.5 temperature, then consumes the items placed on the plinths to increase or decrease those values. It also starts by assuming a range of 0.1 is acceptable in both directions.\n\nThe items that modify these values are as follows:\n- Sand -\u003e Humidity -0.1\n- Sandstone -\u003e Humidity -0.2\n- Netherrack -\u003e Humidity -0.4\n- Lapis -\u003e Humidity +0.1\n- Water Bucket -\u003e Humidity +0.2\n- Lapis Block -\u003e Humidity +0.4\n- Coal -\u003e Temperature +0.1\n- Coal Block -\u003e Temperature +0.2\n- Lava Bucket -\u003e Temperature +0.4\n- Snowball -\u003e Temperature -0.1\n- Snow Block -\u003e Temperature -0.2\n- Ice Block -\u003e Temperature -0.4\n\nOnce you have used the items to reach your desired environment, the ritual will give you a biome from it. If there are multiple biomes with that humidity and temperature, you can use wool to determine the exact one, for up to 17 conflicting biomes. If the ritual cannot find a valid biome, it will default to Plains.\n\nSome cool ones include, but are not limited to:\n- Sky (also known as End) -\u003e Orange Wool\n- Eldritch -\u003e Cyan Wool\n- Eerie -\u003e Light Gray Wool\n- TF Forest -\u003e Pink Wool\n- Sacred Springs -\u003e Yellow Wool\n- Tainted Land -\u003e Purple or Blue Wool\n- Moon -\u003e 0% Humidity, No Wool\n- Mars Flat -\u003e 0% Humidity, White Wool\n- Asteroids -\u003e 0% Humidity, Orange Wool\n- Space -\u003e 0% Humidity, Magenta Wool\n- Toxic Everglades -\u003e 70% Humidity, No Wool\n\n[note]For the biome change to show up properly on the client, you may need to relog.[/note]",
