      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "A key part of CropsNH is improving the stats of your crops. There is almost always a chance for this to occur whenever a new crop grows - whether by self propagation or crossing...\n\n§lGrowth§r:\n§2Improves growth speed§r\n- Increases the number of progress points per growth tick by up to about 525% with some variation depending on the tier of the crop.\n§4Can cause weeds to spawn§r\n- When growth is above 23 (or 7 for Necrobloom), crops will begin spreading weeds and diseases to nearby crops.\n- You can prevent this by either using Weed-EX or by increasing the resistance stat so it\u0027s equal to or above the growth stat.\n\n§lGain§r:\n§2Improves harvest size§r\n- Up to 2.5x per harvest at 31 gain.\n- Has a gain/100 chance of increasing the stack size of any drop by 1.\n\n§lResistance§r:\n§2Improves seed harvest chances§r\n- A resistance of 10 will guarantee a seed drop when harvesting a mature crop with a reinforced spade.\n- This scales by rate of resistance/10:\n  - 20: 2 seeds\n  - 25: 2 seeds + 50% chance for a 3rd\n  - 31: 3 seeds + 10% chance for a 4th\n- A resistance of 31 will guarantee a seed drop even without a spade.\n§2Increases weed resistance§r\n- When a crop\u0027s growth is above 23, resistance will prevent weed spreading as long as it\u0027s greater than or equal to the growth stat.\n§2Improves a crop\u0027s resistance to diseases§r\n- Each point reduces a crop\u0027s chance of becoming infected.\n- With 31 resistance, crops are immune to diseases.\n§2This includes sickness from lack of Nutrient Score, however, the crop still will not grow without the necessary nutrient level being reached.\n",
