      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "To do anything in CropsNH, you first need crop sticks. These will act as the supports for your plants to grow upon. Empty crop sticks can be doubled by right-clicking another crop stick onto them. These double-crop sticks allow you to breed any adjacent mature crops.\n\nAs new species grow on your crop sticks, you can harvest them by right-clicking, which won\u0027t remove the seed. Left-clicking harvests the crop and removes it, potentially dropping a seed depending on the resistance. Spades will help you improve your chances of obtaining seeds when you do this, as will the Resistance trait.\n\n§r§r[note]§l§r§lThe chance to drop a seed from any crop §nwithout a spade§r§l is measured\nas resistance/31. §rSo crops with a maxed resistance stat will always drop a seed when broken.§r[/note]\n\n[warn]Don\u0027t forget to check the seed tooltips or NEI page for the varying types of soil, sub-soil, and other environmental requirements![/warn]\n\n§oIf you\u0027re already an experienced farmhand, collect a single stonelily seed and I\u0027ll let you skip subsequent introductory trainings for now.",
