      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "You will need Xenoxene to make next tier plastic, Radox, or the next tier of SMDs.\n\nGetting the Xenoxene Xenoxsis culture is a bit tricky. The recipe is similar to the General Purpose one. Remember that all recipes in this chain have a low probability of success.\n\nYour first step is to make the Barnardafis culture, then the DNA Sample, and then the Data Orb. If you didn\u0027t grab the saplings and dirt previously (to grow more trees for logs), head back to Barnarda C.\n\nUse the same recipe as for the General Purpose culture, but use the Barnardafis Data Orb instead of Common Yeast. You should get the Barnardafis Plasmid.\n\nFor the next step, use the same recipe again, this time with the TCetiEis Fucus Serratus culture and the Barnardafis Plasmid. This should produce the Xenoxene Xenoxsis culture, with a 38.7% chance of success.\n\nYou should be able to figure out how to make Xenoxene yourself once you have the culture.\n\nOnce you have Xenoxene, you can use the more effective Beam Crafter recipe to get more cultures.\n\n[note]After many years, the transformation recipe now even has NEI support![/note]",
